      },
      "message": "fix(ui): lay a lathe's spindle axis across the viewport\n\nThe work envelope of a lathe is a cylinder about world Z, as the\nturning paths are. Camera::basis_right always crossed the view with\nworld +Z, so world Z could never lie across the screen and the\ncylinder stood vertical.\n\nThe camera now orbits in a ViewFrame (crate::view_frame) chosen from\nthe mounted machine's kind each frame: Mill is the identity, Lathe\nputs world +Z (the spindle axis) to the right and world +X (the\ncross-slide) up. Eye and basis map through one proper rotation, so\ndraw, pick, pan, dolly, the traced-stock eye and the view cube stay on\none basis. Display only: the world, WCS, toolpaths and posted G-code\ndo not change.\n\nFixes #1993\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
